@page "/legal/privacy"
<PageTitle>Privacy Policy — CrowdFund AI</PageTitle>
<div class="page-container py-5" style="max-width:800px;">
    <h1 class="fw-bold">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">Last updated: 9 November 2026</p>
    <div class="cf-card">
        <h5>Data we collect</h5>
        <ul>
            <li>Account data: email, name, role</li>
            <li>KYC documents and verification outcomes (creators)</li>
            <li>Donation and payout transaction metadata (not full card numbers — handled by PayPal)</li>
            <li>Campaign content, expense uploads, chat messages with the AI assistant</li>
            <li>Security logs: IP address, user agent, admin actions</li>
        </ul>
        <h5>How we use data</h5>
        <p>To operate the platform, process payments, prevent fraud, meet legal obligations, and improve safety systems. AI features process campaign and receipt text to produce advisory scores — not to sell personal data.</p>
        <h5>Sharing</h5>
        <p>Payment processors (e.g. PayPal), infrastructure providers, and authorities when required by law. We do not sell personal information.</p>
        <h5>Retention</h5>
        <p>Transaction and audit records are retained as required for financial and dispute purposes. You may request access or deletion subject to legal retention duties.</p>
        <h5>Security</h5>
        <p>Encryption in transit, access controls, rate limiting, and audit logging. No method is 100% secure.</p>
        <h5>Contact</h5>
        <p>privacy@crowdfundai.example</p>
    </div>
</div>
